-- title:
--   Symmetry of the division-polynomial independence unit
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $A$, and $p$ a prime with $p \neq 2$. Assume that $p$ is a unit in $A$ and that the discriminant $W.\Delta$ is a unit in $A$. Let $x_P, y_P, x_Q, y_Q \in A$ be such that $(x_P,y_P)$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)$ satisfy the affine Weierstrass equation of $W$, and such that the $p$-th pre-division polynomial $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi(p)$ (for the integer $p$) vanishes at $x_P$ and at $x_Q$. The quantity [`ModularCurve.indepElt W p x₀ x`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L18) is by definition the product $\prod_{a=1}^{(p-1)/2}\bigl(x\cdot \Psi_a^2(x_0) - \Phi_a(x_0)\bigr)$, the index $a$ running over the integer interval from $1$ to $(p-1)/2$ (natural subtraction and division) and $\Psi_a^2 =$ `W.ΨSq a`, $\Phi_a =$ `W.Φ a` being the usual division polynomials of $W$ evaluated at $x_0$. The assertion is: if $\prod_{a=1}^{(p-1)/2}\bigl(x_Q\,\Psi_a^2(x_P) - \Phi_a(x_P)\bigr)$ is a unit of $A$, then so is $\prod_{a=1}^{(p-1)/2}\bigl(x_P\,\Psi_a^2(x_Q) - \Phi_a(x_Q)\bigr)$.
--
--   Over a field the unit (equivalently, non-vanishing) of [`ModularCurve.indepElt W p x₀ x`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L18) expresses that the point with abscissa $x$ does not lie in the cyclic subgroup generated by the $p$-torsion point with abscissa $x_0$; the statement is the symmetry of this independence condition in the two points, in the form used for Drinfeld bases of level $p$ over an arbitrary base ring. It is invoked in the treatment of full level structures on modular curves, for instance in the determinant computations attached to the diamond and $\Gamma_0$-type actions and in the vanishing criterion for Katz level-$p$ forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isUnit_indepElt_symm.lean

